---
import WorkbenchLayout from "../../../layouts/WorkbenchLayout.astro";
---

<WorkbenchLayout
  title="Workbench Terms | PENGO Workbench"
  description="Terms for using the PENGO Workbench public reference library."
  url="https://pengosystems.com/workbench/terms/"
  active="terms"
  breadcrumb="Workbench Terms"
>
  <article class="wb-content wb-template">
    <p class="wb-type-label">Terms</p>
    <h1>Workbench Terms</h1>
    <p class="wb-lede">
      Terms for using the PENGO Workbench public reference library.
    </p>

    <section class="wb-reading-section">
      <h2>Reference Material</h2>
      <p>
        PENGO Workbench is a public reference library for inspecting AI-facing failure
        surfaces, structural Patterns, diagnostic Lenses, AI-Adjacent Issues, and Check Input outputs.
      </p>
      <p>
        Workbench material is provided for reference, education, analysis, and discussion.
      </p>
      <p>
        Workbench pages may change as the reference library expands.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="wb-reading-section">
      <h2>Not Professional Advice</h2>
      <p>
        Workbench material is not legal, medical, financial, security, compliance,
        procurement, operational, or professional advice.
      </p>
      <p>
        Do not rely on Workbench pages as the sole basis for decisions that require
        professional judgment, formal review, organizational approval, or independent verification.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="wb-reading-section">
      <h2>No Final Determination</h2>
      <p>
        Workbench references may help inspect related structure. They do not prove
        causality, diagnose a model, validate a prompt, score a system, certify a workflow,
        or determine why an AI system failed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="wb-reading-section">
      <h2>Fit Depends on Context</h2>
      <p>
        Workbench references may not fit every system, workflow, model, tool, prompt,
        organization, or use case.
      </p>
      <p>
        You are responsible for deciding whether a Workbench reference applies to your context.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="wb-reading-section">
      <h2>Responsibility for Use</h2>
      <p>
        You are responsible for how you interpret, reuse, cite, adapt, or apply Workbench material.
        PENGO Systems is not responsible for decisions, outputs, actions, workflows, claims, losses,
        or consequences resulting from use of Workbench material, Check Input outputs, Explore Results
        mappings, or related references.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</WorkbenchLayout>
